copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, or sell any part of it.

This file does not take any right away: a public repository with no LICENSE already
defaults to "all rights reserved" under copyright law. It only says so out loud, so
that anyone who finds the repo knows where they stand instead of having to guess.

Two reasons it is written this way rather than as MIT:

  1. The game is built on Axie Infinity lore under the Axie Infinity Builder's
     Program. Some of the source material it draws on is distributed to Builder's
     Program teams under "do not distribute" terms. A permissive licence on this
     repository would read as granting rights over material that is not the
     copyright holder's to grant.

  2. Third-party assets vendored here (fonts, audio, Spine art packages) arrive
     under their own terms, which a repository-wide MIT grant would misstate.

If you want the code opened later, replace this file with the licence you choose and
say so in README.md. Do the asset audit in point 2 first — the code and the assets
may well need different answers.

For permission to use any part of this work, contact the repository owner.
